{
  "format": "fud-bin",
  "notes": [
    "Each case is one value of its type, written as a level of a single slot: a response body.",
    "A type is a primitive by its name, or an object: {\"list\": T}, {\"opt\": T}, {\"map\": [K, V]}, {\"oneOf\": [members]}, {\"fields\": {name: T, ...}} with its fields in order. \"problem\" is the problem level; \"any\" a validator's value.",
    "A value is JSON. A date is its ISO 8601 text, a uuid its text, a key of a map its text. An absent optional is left out, or null.",
    "hex is every byte of the body, two lowercase digits each. A backend speaks fud-bin when it writes each value as its hex and reads each hex back as its value."
  ],
  "cases": [
